  "id": "DrugBank_DB06761 - MONDO_6502",
  "verbalization": "Beractant is implicated in the pathogenesis of Acute Respiratory Distress Syndrome (ARDS) through a chain of indications that link it to Newborn Respiratory Distress Syndrome (NRDS). This relationship is supported by the shared indication of Beractant with NRDS, which in turn is linked to other drugs such as Tyloxapol, Poractant Alfa, and Colfosceril Palmitate, all of which are indicated for ARDS. The evidence suggests that Beractant may exert a therapeutic or pathophysiological effect that is relevant to ARDS, possibly through mechanisms involving respiratory support or modulation of inflammatory responses. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Beractant in the treatment or prevention of ARDS, particularly in the context of neonatal respiratory distress.",
